**Two visual worlds, used deliberately**

*Entry + auth screens (dark)* — Landing, Home, Sign in, Sign up: near-black base with a soft blue top glow and a fine starfield texture, large light-weight display headlines, minimal chrome. Confident, modern, software-y — think a well-funded dev-tool landing page, not a hospital form.

*Clinical workflow screens (light only, no dark mode)* — Patients, New Patient, Consult, Review, Diagnosis: "clinical calm" — precision-instrument feel, quiet and trustworthy. Warm off-white background (`#FAF9F6`), white cards, one accent color only: deep teal (`#0F6E6B`) for actions/links/active states. Titles semibold, never black-weight. One soft shadow only, 16px card radius, 12px button radius, spacing on a 4/8/12/16/24/32 scale.

Tier colors for differential diagnoses are muted, not traffic-light: teal for "most likely," ochre for "expanded differential," oxblood for "can't miss" — thin left border + small label chip, never a full card fill.

A slim amber-on-cream "DEMO" ribbon appears on every clinical screen — legible, understated. Icons: simple line icons only, no emoji anywhere.

**Pages to design**

1. **Landing** (dark) — full-bleed calm intro, product name, tagline, single primary CTA.
2. **Sign in / Sign up** (dark) — minimal email+password form, same dark/glow aesthetic.
3. **Patients list** (light) — patient cards (avatar-initials, name, age/sex, chief complaint, last-consult time), FAB to add patient, designed empty state.
4. **New patient** (light) — single-screen form, floating labels, segmented control, keyboard-safe.
5. **Consult (live recording)** (light) — chat bubbles (doctor left white, patient right teal-tinted), speaker chip per turn, sticky translucent header (name + timer + pulsing record dot), dismissible suggestion cards sliding in above the input, end-consult button.
6. **Review** (light) — transcript continues above; below it a grid of labeled chips (symptoms/duration/history/meds/observations); primary CTA "Analyze."
7. **Diagnosis** (light) — red-flags banner pinned top; three tier sections (Most likely / Expanded / Can't miss) of differential cards (tier border+chip, name, 2-line reasoning, evidence-count badge, accept/dismiss icons); "Suggested workup" checklist; tap a card → evidence bottom sheet (quoted lines with play buttons + guideline excerpt block); "Not yet ruled out" gap-detection section; supportive (never grading) "Assessment alignment" section.

